Z||000021||LZeitgeist||12-28-2001||07:48 AM||||No, the screw in the base doesn't come out that easily - you'd have to remove the entire fender to get to the antenna base to change the screw. <P>I'm sure there's a standard type of 'soft' antenna that will thread to the existing base. I doubt that Fiero antenna bases are threaded differently than any other GM car.||||reg||1
Z||000022||kneebarx||12-28-2001||10:12 AM||||or get one of those real fancy alarms that beep you when your car is being damaged.  Then you can run out with the machete, gobstopper paintball gun, or whatever else to scare them to all kingdom come!||||reg||1
Z||000023||Formula88||12-28-2001||10:20 AM||||Personally, if you intend to intervene with people in the commission of a crime, you d@mn well better be armed with something better than a paintball gun or knife!  Maybe they're just kids being kids.  Maybe not.  Don't set yourself up for a rude awakening by bringing a toy to a gun fight.  If that thought bothers you - you don't need to try intervening in the first place.<P>As for the antennae, you might try to hidden antenna mod.  Do a search for "invisible antenna" or something like that.  Basically, you wire the antenna to the sunroof frame, there is no antenna on the outside of the car.  I'm thinking about it just to clean up the lines of the car some.<P>Remember some important things when dealing with criminals.  Some of them are just punks.  Some of those punks carry guns.  Some of them are stupid enough to shoot you for no reason.  If you run out of your house with a knife in your shorts, you're gonna look mighty stupid lying on the ground in a pool of your own blood with a 9mm hole in your chest, in your underwear, with a knife in your hand.  Personally, I like swords for home defense, but they only work in a defensive situation.  You don't go chasing someone down with a sword, especially if they might have a gun.  Now, if you're hiding around the corner, and that someone comes around the corner with a gun, then a sword can be useful.  Can't pull a trigger with no hands.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000024||Sootah||12-28-2001||02:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WhiteFieroBlur:<BR><B>no all the local ricers are my friend. I do think someone is being a hatter in my town or jelous or something. I got the only custom fiero around that looks nice so I dunno what these ricers think they are doing. I just hope the next time I don't find a brick thru my windshield or something   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Put a brick through their skull... Actually,  with the paintball gun, you don't use gobstoppers. Instead what you do is buy a big case of paintballs and stick them in the freezer for a few hours. When they come again, aim for the ears.<P>Oh, yeah, tear gas. If you do manage to find out who is doing this then just spray a little tear gas into their vents. They won't be able to drive the car for like two weeks. (Now your wondering, how does he know this? Done it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Yes, I am a vengefull bastard. I had a CD player stolen out of my POS cavalier a couple of years ago. As soon as I found out who did it (for sure) I broke their windshield and did the tear gas bit. I let em keep the player.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__tig_sig2.gif">           <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Don't sweat the petty things, and don't pet the sweaty things</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AOL IM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||1
